{
  "summary": "This study investigates how dual twisted interfaces in CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 affect second harmonic generation (SHG). By fabricating nine distinct stacking configurations, the researchers analyzed Raman and photoluminescence data to identify stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses. Atomic-resolution imaging confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice. They developed a framework linking interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization, demonstrating TT-MoS2's potential as a tunable nonlinear optical platform.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dual twisted interfaces in trilayer MoS2 create a supermoiré lattice structure",
    "Stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses modulate SHG intensity",
    "A framework links interface geometry to SHG polarization and intensity"
  ],
  "study_type": "CVD-grown twisted trilayer MoS2 configurations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a structural framework for engineering multi-interface twisted coupling in van der Waals materials to control nonlinear optical responses, advancing tunable second harmonic generation platforms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses residual tumor persistence after high-frequency irreversible electroporation (H-FIRE) for prostate cancer. By identifying DNA damage repair as the key mechanism for reversible cell survival, researchers engineered piezoelectric nanomaterial BOIS. H-FIRE-induced membrane permeability allows BOIS delivery to residual cells. Ultrasound activation triggers BOIS to generate electric fields and reactive oxygen species, causing irreversible cell death through dual mechanisms. This approach significantly enhances tumor eradication by converting reversible injury to irreversible damage.",
  "key_findings": [
    "H-FIRE-induced membrane permeability enables BOIS delivery to residual prostate cancer cells",
    "Ultrasound-activated BOIS produces electric fields and ROS to induce irreversible cell death",
    "The strategy converts reversible tumor injury to irreversible lethal damage, improving eradication"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach establishes a self-reinforcing therapeutic loop where focal ablation delivers nanomaterials to enhance residual tumor destruction, offering a novel mechanism for complete prostate cancer eradication."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated metabolic heterogeneity in small cell lung cancer (SCLC) cell states. Using transcriptomic and metabolomic analyses, it identified universal cysteine dependency across neuroendocrine (NE) and non-NE SCLC states. NE cells with low ASCL1 levels underwent ferroptosis upon cysteine depletion, while ASCL1high cells underwent apoptosis and resisted ferroptosis due to GCH1-mediated BH4/BH2 upregulation. Targeting cysteine and BH4/BH2 synthesis reduced tumor growth in xenografts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SCLC cells exhibit universal cysteine dependency across neuroendocrine and non-neuroendocrine states",
    "ASCL1low NE cells undergo ferroptosis upon cysteine depletion, whereas ASCL1high cells undergo apoptosis and resist ferroptosis",
    "GCH1 transcriptional activation by ASCL1 increases BH4/BH2, conferring ferroptosis resistance"
  ],
  "study_type": "Integrated transcriptomic and metabolomic analyses",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings establish metabolic state as a determinant of cell death susceptibility in SCLC, revealing a mechanism for targeted therapeutic intervention through cysteine and antioxidant pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated sustained insulin-like growth factor-1 (IGF-1) delivery to reverse chronic denervation effects using a long-acting injectable nanoparticle-hydrogel depot. The approach involved encapsulating IGF-1 in poly(ethylene glycol)-b-polycaprolactone nanoparticles within an injectable nanofiber-hydrogel composite. In rats and non-human primates, the system improved grip strength, myelinated axon counts, and muscle cross-sectional area while reducing fibrosis and enhancing reinnervation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Increased grip strength by 29.1% in rats",
    "186.2% rise in myelinated axon counts in rats",
    "57.0% functional recovery improvement in non-human primates"
  ],
  "study_type": "Long-acting injectable nanoparticle-hydrogel depot",
  "scientific_significance": "This biomaterial platform demonstrates sustained protein delivery for chronic denervation treatment, providing a scalable strategy to maintain trophic support during nerve regeneration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates macrophage functional diversity beyond fixed subsets or binary states, emphasizing their integration of developmental origin, tissue environment, and epigenetic factors. Using single-cell genomics and computational models, it demonstrates that macro:phage states arise from modular gene programs. The findings suggest that precise therapeutic interventions require defining disease-specific macrophage states and targeting their underlying regulatory mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Macrophage identity depends on integration of developmental origin, tissue niche, and environmental cues rather than fixed subsets",
    "Macrophage states are defined by modular gene programs rather than discrete labels",
    "Therapeutic interventions need precise targeting of disease-associated macrophage states through spatial and temporal regulation"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances the understanding of macrophage heterogeneity by framing their functional states as dynamic combinations of modular programs, providing a framework for targeted immunomodulatory therapies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of observing distributed cortical circuits during natural behavior using a novel wireless mesoscope called Airscope. The device achieves 4 μm lateral resolution over a 6 mm field of view at 12.5 Hz, weighing 1 gram. It enables high-throughput calcium imaging of up to 8,500 neurons per animal across diverse behavioral paradigms, including social dominance, maze exploration, and fear conditioning. The technology supports concurrent multi-animal recordings and reveals cortical activity patterns linked to behavioral outcomes and spinal-cortical interactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Airscope provides 4 μm lateral resolution across a 6 mm field of view at 12.5 Hz with 1-gram weight",
    "Cortical activity patterns correlate with social dominance and predict competition outcomes between animals",
    "Reward-location-associated activity patterns emerge during maze exploration and spinal-cortical Granger causality is observed during fear conditioning"
  ],
  "study_type": "Wireless mesoscope",
  "scientific_significance": "This technology enables large-scale, cellular-resolution cortical imaging during naturalistic behavior, overcoming previous constraints of tethering and limited field of view for systems neuroscience."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how autologous erythrocyte microparticles enhance antitumour T cell immunity through haem-mediated dendritic cell activation. Using controlled UV irradiation, the researchers generated microparticles that function as potent T helper type 1-skewing adjuvants. In vitro and mouse tumour models, these particles improved cytotoxic T cell responses against tumour antigens while suppressing tumour growth with minimal toxicity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Erythrocyte microparticles generated via UV irradiation act as T helper type 1-skewing adjuvants",
    "Microparticles deliver haem cargo to dendritic cells, elevating lysosomal pH to promote nuclear transport",
    "Haem activates REV-ERB⍺ to suppress peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor gamma, enhancing dendritic cell maturation"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and mouse tumour models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies host-derived erythrocyte microparticles as a novel adjuvant platform that can boost cytotoxic T cell immunity against tumours through haem-mediated dendritic cell activation mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered human Argona:2 (AGO2) to create a modular RNA targeting domain for targeted C-to-U RNA base editing. The approach combined AGO2 with a C-to-U deaminase to develop ALTER, a system that achieves higher editing efficiency on mRNA targets in HEK293T cells than Cas13-based editors while showing comparable or reduced off-target effects and lower immunogenicity potential.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ALTER achieves 1.9-fold higher C-to-U editing efficiency on mRNA targets in HEK293T cells compared to Cas13 editors",
    "Transcriptome-wide RNA-seq indicates similar or lower off-target editing rates than Cas13-based systems",
    "Machine learning predicts ALTER generates fewer immunogenic peptides, supporting potential for deimmunization"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro cell-based study",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes human protein-based RNA editing as a viable alternative to foreign protein systems, potentially enhancing therapeutic safety and specificity in RNA manipulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates TFH cells' role in gut immune tolerance by identifying their production of IL-2 to sustain regulatory T cells in gut-associated lymphoid tissues. Using mouse models, researchers found that TFH-derived IL-2 maintains Treg homeostasis and prevents pathogenic T cell expansion. Mice lacking this IL-2 production developed colitis and multiorgan inflammation, highlighting the necessity of TFH cells for intestinal immune tolerance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TFH cells produce IL-2 at the T cell-B cell border and interfollicular regions to maintain gut Treg homeostasis",
    "Mice without IL-2-producing TFH cells developed colitis and fatal multiorgan inflammation",
    "Antibiotic treatment alleviated pathology, indicating loss of tolerance to commensal antigens drives disease"
  ],
  "study_type": "Mouse model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work reveals a spatially restricted TFH cell-derived IL-2 niche essential for maintaining gut immune tolerance, expanding understanding of how regulatory T cells are sustained in mucosal immunity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates bioresorbable metal-free molecular magnets for untethered organ monitoring. Researchers developed a graphitic carbon nitride-based magnet with high ferromagnetic strength and full bioresorbability. The material, combined with biocompatible polymers, enables catheter-deliverable epicardial patches and injectable hydrogels for cardiac and hepatic monitoring. In porcine trials, it provided continuous ejection fraction tracking over four weeks with benign bioresorption, matching clinical echocardiography standards.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Graphitic carbon nitride-based molecular magnet achieves metallic-level ferromagnetism and full bio:resorbability",
    "Integrated with biocompatible polymers, the material supports catheter-deliverable cardiac patches and injectable hydrogels for multi-organ sensing",
    "In porcine models, the system enabled continuous ejection fraction monitoring over four weeks with benign bioresorption, matching clinical echocardiography standards"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo porcine model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a bioresorbable metal-free molecular magnet system capable of continuous, untethered multi-organ monitoring without tissue interference, advancing non-invasive physiological tracking technology."
}

{
  "summary": "This study identifies cyanobacterial NosH as the first enzyme catalyzing direct prenyl transfer to free guanidine, overcoming guanidine's chemical stability challenges. Structural analysis revealed a two-aspartate clamp mechanism. Plant prenyltransferases were discovered, producing galegine in vitro and in planta via heterologous expression, establishing a novel enzymatic pathway for guanidine alkaloid biosynthesis in plants.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cyanobacterial NosH catalyzes direct prenyl transfer to free guanidine",
    "Structural analysis identified a two-aspartate clamp mechanism for guanidine activation",
    "Plant prenyltransferases produce galegine in vitro and in planta"
  ],
  "study_type": "Structural and mechanistic analysis",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes the first enzymatic pathway for guanidine alkaloid biosynthesis in plants, revealing a conserved prenyltransferase mechanism across bacteria and plants that overcomes guanidine's chemical stability barriers."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how STAT3 acts as a context-dependent transcriptional regulator in antiviral natural killer (NK) cells during mouse cytomegalovirus (MCMV) infection. The research demonstrates STAT3's role in integrating IL-15 and type I interferon signals to drive alternative transcriptional programs via distinct genomic loci, thereby influencing NK cell differentiation and adaptive immune responses based on inflammatory conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "STAT3 integrates IL-15 and type I interferon signals to regulate NK cell differentiation during MCMV infection",
    "STAT3 recruits to distinct genomic loci depending on inflammatory milieu, driving alternative transcriptional programs",
    "STAT3 differentially regulates transcription factors MYB and BLIMP-1 to shape NK cell adaptation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Mouse cytomegalovirus infection model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes STAT3 as a cytokine-sensing transcriptional switch that dynamically modulates immune cell function by responding to environmental inflammatory cues, advancing understanding of context-dependent immune regulation during viral infections."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress inward, suppresses electrode swelling, and enhances Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with reduced expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Heteroatom doping enhances electronic conductivity and interlayer spacing for balanced Li+ kinetics",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro synthesis and electrochemical testing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable strategy for developing practical silicon-carbon anodes with minimal expansion and enhanced cycling stability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how the blood-brain barrier (BBB) selectively transports neuroprotective proteins into the brain. Using bioorthogonal proteomics, researchers identified 191 plasma proteins sampled and 92 permitted across the BBB in healthy conditions. These proteins, enriched for carrier and metabolic functions, target specific brain cell types via receptor-mediated mechanisms. Early Alzheimer's disease models show reduced APOA1 and increased SERPINA1 uptake, while hepatic APOA1 overexpression rescues synaptic and behavioral deficits in 5xFAD mice.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The healthy BBB samples 191 plasma proteins and permits 92 into the brain parenchyma.",
    "Neuroprotective proteins like APOA1 home to astrocytes and SERPINA1 to microglia via receptor-mediated mechanisms.",
    "Early Alzheimer's disease models exhibit reduced APOA1 and increased SERPINA1 uptake, with hepatic APOA1 overexpression rescuing synaptic and behavioral deficits."
  ],
  "study_type": "Bioorthogonal proteomics",
  "scientific_significance": "This work redefines the BBB as a selective interface that recruits circulatory neuroprotective proteins to maintain brain health, highlighting a critical pathway for Alzheimer's disease pathogenesis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates programmable engineering of complex tissue curvatures using a bio-Kirigami system. The approach combines a photocrosslinked hydrogel with tunable degradation/swelling and a rigid hydrogel frame for spatial patterning. The system enables cell-laden constructs to transform into tissue-like structures with intricate curvatures, maintaining structural integrity post-frame removal. The findings demonstrate a versatile method for replicating native tissue geometries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A photocrosslinked hydrogel with tunable degradation and swelling behavior drives shape transformation",
    "Spatial patterning via sequential photolithography encodes localized swelling differentials for controlled deformation",
    "Engineered tissue constructs retain structural integrity after frame removal under tissue-specific culture conditions"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro tissue engineering model",
  "scientific_significance": "This strategy advances the field by enabling programmable recapitulation of native tissue curvatures through dynamic morphogenesis in engineered constructs."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how NF-κB phosphorylation at Ser276 regulates enhancer selection during inflammatory responses. Using Rela Ser276Ala mutant macrophages, it found phosphorylation is essential for recruiting NF-κB to nucleosome-occluded enhancers, enabling chromatin opening and inflammatory gene expression. Mutant cells showed impaired responses to bacterial infection but maintained antiviral defenses and endotoxin resistance. The results reveal functional partitioning of enhancer architectures in NF-κB-mediated inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Phosphorylation of NF-κB p65 at Ser276 is required for recruitment to nucleosome-occluded enhancers lacking pre-bound transcription factors",
    "This phosphorylation enables histone acetylation and chromatin opening at latent enhancers to activate inflammatory genes",
    "Rela Ser276Ala mice exhibited resistance to endotoxin shock but susceptibility to bacterial infection"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro macrophage model with Rela Ser276Ala mutation",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that NF-κB phosphorylation at Ser276 functionally partitions enhancer architectures, revealing a mechanism for distinct inflammatory gene programs through chromatin accessibility regulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates using generative protein design to create enantioselective artificial metalloenzymes for photocatalysis. By de novo designing protein scaffolds that bind metal polypyridine photocatalysts, the researchers achieved highly enant. The evolved proteins enabled efficient, recyclable catalysis with racemic metal complexes, extended excited-state lifetimes, and controlled stereoselectivity through substrate organization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "De novo protein scaffolds selectively bind metal polypyridine photocatalysts",
    "Directed evolution produced highly enantioselective photocatalysts with high turnover and recyclability",
    "Protein environment extends photocatalyst excited-state lifetime and controls stereoselectivity via substrate organization"
  ],
  "study_type": "Generative protein design with directed evolution",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes de novo protein design as a general strategy for creating functional scaffolds for synthetic metal complexes lacking natural protein partners, advancing asymmetric photocatalysis through controlled stereoselectivity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates hydrogel-based delivery of AS2863619 to induce regulatory T cells for bone regeneration. The hydrogel system, incorporating laponite nanoparticles, enables sustained release of the cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor. In a calvarial bone defect model, it promoted Treg activation, reduced inflammation, and enhanced bone repair with complete defect bridging in some cases. The approach provides spatiotemporal control without ex vivo cell manipulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AS-loaded hydrogels induced dose-dependent regulatory T cell activation in bone defects",
    "Reduced pro-inflammatory macrophage responses and enhanced bone regeneration",
    "AS-laponite hydrogels achieved complete defect bridging in some cases"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo calvarial bone defect model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a scalable method for localized immunomodulation via Treg induction without cell manipulation, advancing tissue repair strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates using genetic code expansion with noncanonical amino acids (ncAAs) to enable plant-directed control of bacterial activity. By engineering Bacillus subtilis to respond to O-methyl-L-tyrosine (OMY), the researchers demonstrate that plant-derived OMY can trigger specific bacterial responses. The approach shows tissue-specific induction of microbial activity through plant biosynthesis of OMY, providing a programmable mechanism for plant-microbe interactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Engineered B. subtilis strains suppress in-frame amber stop codons when OMY is present",
    "Arabidopsis, tomato, and poplar biosynthesize OMY to stimulate bacterial gene expression",
    "Plant-derived OMY enables tissue-specific, inducible control of microbial activity"
  ],
  "study_type": "Genetic code expansion with orthogonal aminoacyl-tRNA synthetase/tRNA pairs",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes noncanonical amino acids as a programmable tool for inducing specific microbial responses in plant-associated bacteria, advancing strategies for controlled plant-microbe interactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how spatial confinement in germinal centers (GCs) influences B cell clonal diversity and immunodominance. Using mice with impaired GC confinement due to Gα13 deficiency, researchers observed reduced GC clonal diversity and increased immunodominance when GCs were deconfined. Spatial B cell receptor sequencing showed greater clonal crossover between neighboring GCs in dispersal conditions, leading to decreased overall repertoire diversity and stronger preference for accessible epitopes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Deconfined germinal centers exhibited minimal clonal diversification compared to confined settings",
    "Increased clonal crossover between neighboring germinal centers in deconfined conditions",
    "Reduced overall B cell repertoire diversity with heightened immunodominance in deconfined lymph nodes"
  ],
  "study_type": "Mouse models with Gα13 deficiency",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that spatial confinement in germinal centers modulates antibody breadth by restricting dominant clone expansion and preserving unique clonal trajectories during immune responses."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates integrating non-volatile memory into magnonic circuits using spin waves. It proposes a strategy leveraging static magnetization states in waveguiding elements within zero-field magnetic insulators. The approach enables efficient control of spin-wave propagation paths via magnetization switching, suggesting potential for low-energy, self-contained magnonic nano-circuits.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Static magnetization states in waveguiding elements enable non-volatile memory integration",
    "Magnetization switching controls spin-wave propagation paths efficiently",
    "Low-energy selective magnet:ing switching is achievable in zero-field magnonic networks"
  ],
  "study_type": "Theoretical proposal",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a foundational method for integrating memory directly into magnonic circuits, advancing the feasibility of self-contained spin-wave based nanoscale computing systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines recent high-impact publications across Science journals to identify patterns in research output and thematic trends. The analysis reveals a focus on interdisciplinary work and rapid advancements in biotechnology, with notable increases in climate-related studies. These findings suggest evolving priorities in scientific communication and the growing importance of cross-disciplinary collaboration.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Increased emphasis on interdisciplinary research in recent high-impact publications",
    "Rapid advancements in biotechnology highlighted in the analysis",
    "Notable rise in climate-related scientific studies"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The research provides insights into shifting scientific priorities and the expanding role of interdisciplinary approaches in addressing complex global challenges."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates glycosylation mechanisms in γδ T17 cells using single-cell RNA sequencing. It identifies that type 3 γδ T17 cells depend on MGAT1-MGAT5-mediated branched N-glycosylation for IL-17A commitment. The absence of branched N-glycans promotes a pro-inflammatory phenotype, Vγ4+ subset shift, and innate-like properties, correlating with severe psoriasis and autoimmune diseases. Glycan supplementation reprograms these cells toward reduced pathogenicity, revealing N-glycans as an immune checkpoint.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Type 3 γδ T17 cells require MGAT1-MGAT5-mediated branched N-glycosylation for IL-17A commitment",
    "Deficiency in branched N-glycans drives pro-inflammatory phenotypes, Vγ4+ subset shifts, and innate-like properties",
    "Glycan supplementation reprograms γδ T cells to reduce pathogenicity, highlighting N-glycans as an immune checkpoint"
  ],
  "study_type": "single-cell RNA sequencing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies N-glycans as a previously unrecognized immune checkpoint regulating γδ T cell pathogenicity, providing a novel therapeutic target for autoimmune disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a plasmonic coacervate platform for detecting polystyrene micro/nanoplastics (MNPs) in water. The platform uses liquid-liquid phase separation to form charged droplets that spontaneously capture PS MNPs with high enrichment rates (99.4% for nano, 91.1% for micro). It integrates silver nanoparticles to create SERS hotspots, achieving an enhancement factor of 2.72 × 109 and detecting PS at 1–10 ng/mL. The method successfully recovers MNPs from environmental samples and food-contact materials.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Spontaneous capture of polystyrene MNPs with 99.4% enrichment for nano and 91.1% for microscale particles",
    "SERS enhancement factor of 2.72 × 109 enabling detection at 1–10 ng/mL for PS MNPs",
    "Recovery rates of 87–108% for PS MNPs in tap and river water, and detection from food-contact materials"
  ],
  "study_type": "Plasmonic coacervate platform using liquid-liquid phase separation",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a sensitive, rapid method for detecting micro/nanoplastics in environmental and food-contact contexts through spontaneous sequestration and plasmonic amplification."
}
